   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Localization/Away/Basic.lean:93: `lemma surj (z : S) : \u2203 (n : \u2115) (a : R), z * algebraMap R S x ^ n = algebraMap R S a`. The goal after the `rw` chain has the shape `\u2026 * (x i * (\u03d6 : K) ^ n) \u2208 \ud835\udcaa[K]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/MeasureTheory/Group/BoundedLineSections.lean",
   "fix": "Make the bridge explicit. First rewrite `ha` into coercion form with a named `algebraMap`-equals-coercion simp lemma for subrings, for example `simp only [map_pow, <that lemma>] at ha`. Then finish with `exact ha \u25b8 a.2` or `rw [ha]; exact a.2`. Alternatively, add a comment explaining the definitional equality.",
   "issue": "`ha \u25b8 a.2` silently relies on definitional equality. `IsLocalization.Away.surj` gives `ha : x i * algebraMap \ud835\udcaa[K] K \u03d6 ^ n = algebraMap \ud835\udcaa[K] K a`. But the goal is stated with `(\u03d6 : K) ^ n`, and `a.2 : (a : K) \u2208 \ud835\udcaa[K]` is stated with `\u2191a`. Neither form matches `ha` syntactically, so the `\u25b8` closes only because `algebraMap \ud835\udcaa[K] K` unfolds to `Subtype.val`.",
   "line": 84
  }
 ],
